---
layout: base.njk
title: Independent Mac apps & browser tools
description: Meet RelayByte, the independent software studio of Kyle Reddoch. Discover Trayage for Mac, StylePort for Safari, and Drift for Chrome. All available now.
home: true
ogVideo: true
---
<section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Independent software, made in Texas</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Good software.<br><span class="accent-text">Less friction.</span></h1>
      <p>A tidier Mac. A browser that feels like yours. Small, thoughtful apps for the things you do every day.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-dark" href="#apps">Meet the apps <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/blog/' | url }}">Read the blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="studio-visual">
      <button class="brand-art" type="button" aria-label="RelayByte logo card" disabled>
        <span class="brand-art-tilt"><span class="brand-art-spinner">
          <span class="brand-art-face brand-art-front">
            <span class="art-label" aria-hidden="true">SMALL STUDIO. USEFUL SOFTWARE.</span>
            <img src="{{ '/assets/brand/relaybyte-symbol-orange.svg' | url }}" alt="" width="512" height="512">
            <span class="art-foot"><span aria-hidden="true">EST. IN TEXAS</span><span class="art-cta" id="brand-card-action" hidden><span class="art-action-text">Give it a spin</span><span class="art-action-icon" aria-hidden="true">↻</span></span></span>
          </span>
          <span class="brand-art-face brand-art-back" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ '/assets/brand/relaybyte-symbol-orange.svg' | url }}" alt="" width="512" height="512"></span>
        </span></span>
      </button>
      <span class="visual-caption">Made by a person. Made to be useful.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <a class="release-strip" href="{{ '/apps/styleport/' | url }}">
    <img src="{{ '/assets/apps/styleport.png' | url }}" alt="" width="36" height="36">
    <span class="release-label">Now on the Mac App Store</span>
    <span class="release-title">StylePort for Safari <span class="release-description">— free, with every feature included.</span></span>
    <span class="release-action">Meet StylePort <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
  </a>
</section>
<section class="apps-section shell" id="apps" aria-labelledby="apps-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The collection</p><h2 id="apps-title">Small apps. Useful every day.</h2></div>
    <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/apps/' | url }}">All apps <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
  {% include 'app-catalog.njk' %}
</section>
<section class="studio-section shell" aria-label="From the studio">
  <div class="maker-note" aria-labelledby="maker-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">The person behind the apps</p>
    <h2 id="maker-title">Small studio. Personal touch.</h2>
    <p>I’m Kyle, an independent developer in Texas. I build the apps, sweat the details, and answer your emails. My work in cybersecurity shapes how I think about privacy and control.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">Meet the maker <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="studio-journal" aria-labelledby="journal-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="journal-title">The work behind the apps.</h2><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/blog/' | url }}">All notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    {% set postList = collections.blog.slice(0, 1) %}{% include 'post-list.njk' %}
    <a class="journal-rss" href="{{ '/blog/feed.xml' | url }}">Follow via RSS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="home-faq shell" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</p><h2 id="faq-title">Good to know.</h2><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/support/' | url }}">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  <div class="faq-list">{% for item in faq %}<details><summary>{{ item.question }}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{{ item.answer }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div>
</section>
